course: dictionary
lesson: 5824
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «I'm not your personal maid!» The speaker is fed up with tidying up for everyone, so maid here means a person whose job is to clean and do housework.
explain: Read the words around the word to choose its meaning. In «The fair maid waited by the river, singing softly», the old-fashioned story and the word fair show that maid means a young woman. At a wedding, «the maid of honour gave a speech» tells you it means a helper for the bride.
explain: Always check your choice. Swap the meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have probably got it right. If it does not, try a different meaning.
fact: Maid has more than one meaning, so check the context before you decide.
fact: «Maid» can mean a woman whose job is to clean and do housework in a hotel or house.
fact: In old stories, «maid» means a girl or young unmarried woman, as in «a fair maid».
fact: A bridesmaid or maid of honour is a girl or woman who helps the bride at a wedding.
fact: «Housekeeper» is a more polite word than «maid» for a hotel room cleaner.
exercise: «The hotel maid cleaned our room every morning.» What does maid mean here? | *A woman who cleans and does housework | A young girl in a fairy tale | A cupboard for brooms | A bride's helper at a wedding
exercise: «The fair maid waited by the river, singing softly.» What does maid mean in this old story? | *A young girl or young unmarried woman | A kind of bird | A cleaner in a hotel | A bridesmaid
exercise: Mia's cousin is the maid of honour at the wedding. What is her job? | To hand out the invitations | To cook the wedding cake | To clean the church | *To help the bride on her big day
test: «I'm not your personal maid!» What does the speaker mean? | *They are fed up with tidying up for everyone | They want a new job at a wedding | They are very happy to help | They are a princess in a castle
test: Which word is a more polite choice for a hotel room cleaner? | Bridesmaid | Maid | *Housekeeper | Old maid
exam: «The maid of honour gave a speech at the wedding.» What does maid mean here? | A young girl in a fairy tale | *A bridesmaid, who helps the bride | A hotel cleaner | A woman who does housework at home
